     "before": "The showing is there — line 37 has Mr Bingley dancing every dance — but line 38 answers it with 'such amiable qualities must speak for themselves', which declines the plain telling this half-claims.",
     "after": "Lines 53 to 56 and 65 to 69 give Mr Darcy's own words to Mr Bingley, so the passage states the contrary. The child remembers the room's verdict at lines 42 and 43 and forgets the talk Elizabeth overhears."
